# Notion Time Tracker — Project Conventions

Read `AI_PROJECT_GUIDE.md` at the project root for full architecture, API reference, and data flow documentation.

## Stack

- **Backend**: Node.js + Express 5, SQLite, @notionhq/client
- **Frontend**: React 19, Vite 6, Tailwind CSS 4, React Router 7, Axios
- **Deployment**: Docker Compose (nginx fronts the frontend in prod)

## Key Conventions

- Timestamps are stored as **real UTC** ISO strings. Day boundaries, timeline positions and midnight splitting use the **display timezone** in `Settings.timeZone` (default Pacific/Auckland, editable in the app). Go through `frontend/src/utils/timeUtils.js` / `backend/src/utils/time.js` — never the browser's zone or `getUTC*` for display.
- Currency is **NZD** with **15% GST**. Billing rounds time up to 0.25h increments.
- Notion sync is manual (`POST /api/sync/notion`). Never add auto-sync without discussion. After a sync the Navbar fires a sync-complete event (`utils/syncEvents.js`); pages showing synced data refetch on it.
- The app is single-user, behind one password (`APP_PASSWORD` → stateless HMAC tokens; unset = no auth in local dev).

## Billing

- Bill maths and the "what to invoice, and when" rules live in `backend/src/services/billing.js` (source of truth; `frontend/src/utils/billingUtils.js` mirrors the maths for previews).
- Hourly work is billed **per time entry** (`TimeEntries.billId`), so ongoing tasks can be billed repeatedly. Fixed prices bill once (`Tasks.beenBilled`) or through a payment split (`TaskInstallments`).
- Bills have a `kind`: `invoice`, `external` (already billed elsewhere) or `waived` (written off). All mark work billed; undo = delete the bill. Waived never counts as billed money.
- Projects set when to invoice (as soon as done, or a monthly pay-run cutoff); tasks can override with an invoice date.
- SQLite migrations use `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` with silent no-op in `database.js`.
- Frontend proxies `/api` to the backend (Vite in dev, nginx in prod).

## Sync Behaviour

- Sync fetches only active tasks (Status = "To Do" or "Doing") from Notion.
- Tasks no longer returned by Notion are marked "Done" locally so they leave the Quick Start list.
- Notion property names are **exact-match** (e.g. "Task Name", "Project Link", "Deadline").

## Timeline Component

`TimelineView.jsx` is the most complex component. After changes, add an entry to the version log comment at the top of the file (`// v1.x — <description>`).

Test drag, resize, create, and click-to-select (Resume / Delete bar, incl. on very narrow entries) after any timeline edit.
